# Figure 8 - Omega (spin-orbit) potential energy curves of RaS
# Londono & Perez-Rios, "Electronic properties of the Radium-monochalcogenides
# RaX (X = O,S,Se) and RaO+/- ions"
#
# Source files: Converged_pes/{X1S_0, a3P_0+, a3P_1, a3P_2, A1P_1, B1S_0}_norm_cm.txt
# Energies already in cm^-1 in the source, referenced to the X1Sigma+_0+ minimum.
#
# ###################################################################
# # PROVENANCE WARNING - THESE ARE NOT CALCULATION OUTPUT.          #
# # They carry the signature of values read off a plot.  Replace    #
# # them with the Pauli-Breit output before depositing.             #
# ###################################################################
#
# The evidence:
#   1. QUANTISATION.  In five of the six files every energy is an exact integer
#      multiple of q = 3750/88 = 42.613636 cm^-1, to a relative deviation below
#      1e-14.  Energies converted from hartree do not land on a rational lattice.
#      a3Pi_0+ is the exception and lies off that lattice.
#   2. NO COMMON GRID IN THE SOURCE.  The six states were sampled at slightly
#      different internuclear distances - see the note on the R column below.
#      A spin-orbit calculation diagonalises one matrix per geometry, so every
#      state comes out on the same R grid, as the RaO files do.
#   3. SPARSE, IRREGULAR SAMPLING.  17-19 points per state, unevenly spaced.
#   4. SYSTEMATIC OFFSET.  Every minimum sits 13-22 cm^-1 below the Table VII
#      value, and the X1Sigma+_0+ minimum falls at R = 2.651 A against 2.691 A
#      published - 0.04 A out, far worse than the other five states.
#
# THE R COLUMN
#   The six source files do not share an R grid, so one had to be built.  The
#   108 sampled distances fall into 19 well-separated groups: within a group the
#   values span at most 0.0053 A, while neighbouring groups are an order of
#   magnitude further apart, and no state contributes two points to any group.
#   That is the scatter expected of one nominal distance read six times, so each
#   group is one row here and column 1 is the group mean.  The largest departure
#   of any state's own R from the tabulated value is 0.0029 A.  ENERGIES ARE
#   UNCHANGED - every value below is reproduced exactly as supplied, with no
#   interpolation.  Cells where a state has no point in that group are 'nan'
#   (6 of 114).
#
# Columns
#   1  R              nominal internuclear separation   [Angstrom]
#   2  X1Sigma+_0+    [cm^-1]
#   3  a3Pi_0+        [cm^-1]
#   4  a3Pi_1         [cm^-1]
#   5  a3Pi_2         [cm^-1]
#   6  A1Pi_1         [cm^-1]
#   7  B1Sigma+_0+    [cm^-1]
#
# The rows of the source X1S_0 file were not sorted by R (the R = 3.704 point
# preceded R = 3.503); they are sorted here.
#
# Per-state summary, against Table VII of the paper:
#   state          n   Rmin   Re pub |     Emin    Te pub | on q-lattice | nan
#   X1Sigma+_0+   19  2.651   2.691 |       0.0      0.00 |         yes |  0
#   a3Pi_0+       18  3.001   3.010 |    7978.7   7999.12 |          NO |  1
#   a3Pi_1        18  3.001   2.996 |    7670.5   7692.73 |         yes |  1
#   a3Pi_2        17  3.001   3.006 |    7627.8   7650.27 |         yes |  2
#   A1Pi_1        18  3.001   3.019 |    8224.4   8239.94 |         yes |  1
#   B1Sigma+_0+   18  2.701   2.709 |   12741.5  12754.25 |         yes |  1
#
# Note: the RaS Omega manifold here has six states.  The RaO calculation
# resolves seven, the extra one being a3Pi_0-, which has no counterpart file
# for RaS and no row in Table VII for either molecule.
#
# Extracted 2026-09-25
